  "grid_resolution_caveat": "the frozen lambda grid has NO point between 1e-4 and 1e-2, so a grid lambda* of 1e-2 localises the true crossing only to two decades and is an UPPER BOUND on it. The continuous column is what the linear identity gives exactly.",
  "AM_10_b_both_normalizations": "the statistic here is a ratio of a dispersion to a range, so max(|X|,s_X) and |X| normalizations do not apply to it; the underlying sd and range are both reported so either can be formed."
